course: dictionary
lesson: 6290
title: One word, many meanings: moon
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which one is meant. «The full moon lit up the garden.» The clues are lit up and garden, so moon means the big round object that shines at night.
explain: «Jupiter has many moons.» Now the sentence is about a planet, not the sky above us. A moon here is a natural object that goes around another planet. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Jupiter has many natural objects that go around it" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Moon can also be a verb, but this use is rare. To moon around means to wander about lazily or dreamily. If you read that someone spent the afternoon mooning around the house, the clue is how they move, not the sky.
fact: The Moon, with a capital M, means the one that goes around the Earth.
fact: A moon, with a small m, can be a natural object that goes around another planet, as in «Jupiter has many moons».
fact: The Moon goes around the Earth about once a month and shines at night by reflecting sunlight.
fact: In 1609-1610 Galileo's homemade telescope showed moons going round Jupiter.
fact: Phrases: «once in a blue moon» means very rarely, and «over the moon» means very happy.
exercise: «The full moon lit up the garden.» What does moon mean here? | A lazy, dreamy walk | A small telescope | A planet that goes around the Sun | * The big round object that shines at night
exercise: «Jupiter has many moons.» What does moons mean here? | Stars that twinkle in the night | * Natural objects that go round a planet | Rockets that fly into space | Clouds that hide the sky
exercise: Which phrase means very happy? | Full moon | New moon | * Over the moon | Once in a blue moon
test: «Isaac Newton explained that gravity keeps the Moon going around the Earth.» What does the Moon go around in this sentence? | * The Earth | A cloud | The Sun | Jupiter
test: «In 1970 an oxygen tank exploded on Apollo 13 on the way to the Moon.» Where was Apollo 13 going? | Around Jupiter | Under the sea | * To the Moon | To the bottom of a lake
exam: Which meaning of moons fits «Galileo's telescope showed moons going round Jupiter»? | Sunlight reflected from water | Dreamy, lazy walks | * Natural objects that go round a planet | Lights in the night sky
